// A tagged sum, eliminated by `case`.
//
// Two bidirectional-typing rules surface in this file's shape:
//
//   * injections only *check* -- from `Inl(42)` alone the other summand
//     (`String` here) is not inferable, so the injection carries a type
//     ascription;
//   * a one-part function type annotation (`-> F Integer` below) is enough
//     context for a check-only `case` body.
//
// So the idiomatic shape for a case-bodied function is a single annotated
// function definition: state the result type in the header, then write the
// computation body directly.
def pick() -> F Integer {
  case (Inl(42) : Integer + String) {
    Inl(x) => ret (x + 1),
    Inr(s) => ret 0
  }
}

pick()

// The harness checks:
//@ expect: clean
//@ expect-def: pick
//@ expect-last-value: 43
